DOCK_SAFETY_LIMITS=Safety limits
HEADING_SAFETY_LIMITS=SAFETY LIMITS
MSG_SAFETY_ADMIN_ONLY=Only administrators can change the safety limits.
MSG_SAFETY_INTRO=These limits live in the server, so every app and every window is held to the same ones. A value left empty in a model's row uses the default row. The server also checks every number against its own ceilings.
GROUP_SAFETY_ARMING=Arming of the jog and reservations
LBL_SAFETY_ARM_REQUIRED=The jog has to be armed before it moves a robot
HINT_SAFETY_ARM_REQUIRED=Off by default. When on, a jog without a valid arming is refused by the server.
LBL_SAFETY_ARM_TTL=How long an arming lasts (seconds)
LBL_SAFETY_BETWEEN=between
LBL_SAFETY_REQUIRE_CONTROLLER=A reservation has to name its controller (window or device)
HINT_SAFETY_REQUIRE_CONTROLLER=Off by default. When on, the server refuses a reservation that does not name one.
LBL_SAFETY_AUDIT_MOTION=How often the jog stream is written to the audit record (seconds)
HINT_SAFETY_AUDIT_MOTION=Play, pause, stop, trajectory, table, speed, tool, valve and pump commands are always recorded. A stream of jog commands is recorded at most once per account and robot in this time; 0 leaves the jog stream out of the audit record.
GROUP_SAFETY_LIMITS=Limits by model
HINT_SAFETY_CEILINGS=Ceilings of the server (relative jog / absolute jog / bed):
