PLANNING_TITLE=Planning and operation
PLANNING_INTRO=Read-only views and dry runs. Nothing here moves a robot, queues a job or installs a version.
PLANNING_SIM_TITLE=Plan simulation
PLANNING_SIM_HELP=Paste a plan as JSON (steps and, optionally, constraints). The planner checks it step by step on a simulated clock.
PLANNING_SIM_RUN=Simulate
PLANNING_SIM_INVALID_REQUEST=That is not a plan: it must be a JSON object with a non-empty list of steps.
PLANNING_SIM_ACCEPTED=Accepted: the plan breaks none of the declared rules.
PLANNING_SIM_REJECTED=Rejected: the plan breaks the rules listed below.
PLANNING_SIM_UNCHECKED=Not shown: part of the plan could not be checked (for example the orientation of the tool). This is not an acceptance.
PLANNING_SIM_UNCHECKED_LIST=Not checked
PLANNING_TRAJ_RUN=Check as a trajectory
PLANNING_TRAJ_HELP=Asks the kinematic replica, through the planner, whether the moves are reachable and within the limits. It never executes anything.
PLANNING_SIM_NOT_EXECUTED=Nothing was executed or queued: this is a dry run.
PLANNING_SIM_VIOLATIONS=Broken rules
PLANNING_SIM_TIMELINE=Timeline (simulated)
PLANNING_SIM_MAKESPAN=Total simulated time
PLANNING_OFF=This function is switched off in the service.
PLANNING_FORBIDDEN=Your account may not use this function.
PLANNING_UNREACHABLE=The service does not answer.
PLANNING_NETWORK=The server does not answer.
PLANNING_MALFORMED=The answer is not the one expected, so it is not shown.
PLANNING_HTTP=The service answered with an error.
PLANNING_INVALID=The service refused the request: 
PLANNING_ETA_TITLE=Estimates of the job dispatcher
PLANNING_ETA_HELP=When each job that has not ended is expected to start and end. It assigns nothing.
PLANNING_ETA_LOAD=Read the estimates
PLANNING_ETA_NO_ESTIMATE=No estimate
PLANNING_ETA_DRAIN=The queue is expected to be empty in
PLANNING_ETA_EMPTY=No unfinished jobs.
PLANNING_RUL_TITLE=Remaining useful life
PLANNING_RUL_HELP=Days until the trend of a list of scores reaches a limit. It is an estimate of a trend, not a guarantee.
PLANNING_RUL_POINTS=Points, one per line: seconds, score
PLANNING_RUL_LIMIT=Limit
PLANNING_RUL_RUN=Estimate
PLANNING_RUL_INVALID=Write at least one point per line as "seconds, score" (at most 1000) and a numeric limit.
PLANNING_RUL_INSUFFICIENT_DATA=Not enough points for an estimate.
PLANNING_RUL_NOT_RISING=The scores are not rising.
PLANNING_RUL_LIMIT_REACHED=The limit has already been reached.
PLANNING_RUL_ESTIMATED=Estimated days to the limit
PLANNING_TRAIN_TITLE=Version train (reader)
PLANNING_TRAIN_HELP=Open the file written by `train plan --json` of the updater. It is only shown: nothing is installed from here.
PLANNING_TRAIN_LOAD=Open a train plan
PLANNING_TRAIN_INVALID=That file is not the output of `train plan --json` (version 1).
PLANNING_TRAIN_OK=The train has no problems.
PLANNING_TRAIN_PROBLEMS=Problems
PLANNING_TRAIN_INSTALL=install
PLANNING_TRAIN_UPDATE=update
PLANNING_TRAIN_DOWNGRADE=downgrade
PLANNING_TRAIN_KEEP=keep
PLANNING_TRAIN_BLOCKED=blocked
PLANNING_DL_TITLE=Switches of the data lake
PLANNING_DL_HELP=Read from the data lake itself. They are start-up options of its service, so they are shown here and changed there.
PLANNING_DL_WINDOWS=Window statistics
PLANNING_DL_ON=on
PLANNING_DL_OFF=off
PLANNING_DL_UNKNOWN=unknown
PLANNING_DL_DOWNSAMPLING=Downsampling: not shown here yet.
ECOHEALTH_TITLE=Ecosystem health
ECOHEALTH_DESC=The state of each service of the ecosystem, the version it reports against the version expected, and the days left of the TLS certificate of the server. It only reads; nothing here starts or stops a service.
ECOHEALTH_LOADING=Loading...
ECOHEALTH_REFRESH=Refresh
ECOHEALTH_LOAD_ERROR=The health of the ecosystem could not be loaded.
ECOHEALTH_UNSUPPORTED=This server does not offer the health of the ecosystem, or an administrator has not turned it on in Server Admin.
ECOHEALTH_FORBIDDEN=Your account may not read the health of the ecosystem.
ECOHEALTH_NOT_AVAILABLE=The server could not scan the services of the ecosystem.
ECOHEALTH_FILTERS=Filter services
ECOHEALTH_FILTER_ALL=All
ECOHEALTH_FILTER_OK=Ok
ECOHEALTH_FILTER_DEGRADED=Degraded
ECOHEALTH_FILTER_DOWN=Down
ECOHEALTH_FILTER_UNKNOWN=Unknown
ECOHEALTH_FILTER_DRIFT=Other version
ECOHEALTH_STATE_OK=Ok
ECOHEALTH_STATE_DEGRADED=Degraded
ECOHEALTH_STATE_DOWN=Down
ECOHEALTH_STATE_UNKNOWN=Unknown
ECOHEALTH_REASON_HEALTH_OK=Answers its health check
ECOHEALTH_REASON_HEALTH_DEGRADED=Answers, but reports itself degraded
ECOHEALTH_REASON_HEALTH_FAILED=Answers, but reports a failure
ECOHEALTH_REASON_HTTP_ERROR=Answers its health path with an error
ECOHEALTH_REASON_UNREACHABLE=Does not answer
ECOHEALTH_REASON_UNREACHABLE_UNIT_ACTIVE=Its unit runs but it does not answer
ECOHEALTH_REASON_REACHABLE_UNIT_NOT_ACTIVE=Answers although its unit is not active
ECOHEALTH_REASON_UNIT_ACTIVE=Its unit is active
ECOHEALTH_REASON_UNIT_STARTING=Its unit is starting
ECOHEALTH_REASON_UNIT_FAILED=Its unit has failed
ECOHEALTH_REASON_UNIT_INACTIVE=Its unit is not running
ECOHEALTH_REASON_NO_SIGNAL=No signal to read
ECOHEALTH_REASON_PROBE_ERROR=The check itself failed
ECOHEALTH_VERSION_EXPECTED=Expected
ECOHEALTH_VERSION_REPORTED=Reports
ECOHEALTH_VERSION_UNKNOWN=unknown
ECOHEALTH_DRIFT_BADGE=Other version
ECOHEALTH_LAST_SEEN=Last answer {ago} ago
ECOHEALTH_NEVER_SEEN=No answer since the server started
ECOHEALTH_LATENCY={ms} ms
ECOHEALTH_NO_SERVICES=No service of the ecosystem was found.
ECOHEALTH_NO_MATCH=No service matches this filter.
ECOHEALTH_CERT_OK=The TLS certificate of the server is valid for {days} more days.
ECOHEALTH_CERT_EXPIRING=The TLS certificate of the server expires in {days} days ({date}).
