ECOHEALTH_WARNING_CERTIFICATE_EXPIRED=The TLS certificate of the server has expired.
ECOHEALTH_WARNING_CERTIFICATE_UNREADABLE=The TLS certificate of the server could not be read.
LBL_SECURITY_ECOHEALTH=Health of the ecosystem
LBL_SECURITY_ECOHEALTH_ENABLED=Let operators and administrators read the health of the services (GET /api/ecosystem/health)
LBL_SECURITY_ECOHEALTH_HELP=Off by default: the route then answers as if it did not exist. When on, it lists each service with its state, the version it reports and the days left of the TLS certificate; only administrators also see ports and units.
LBL_SECURITY_TWINRELAY=Live state of the twin
LBL_SECURITY_TWINRELAY_ENABLED=Let the panels follow the live state of the twin through the server (WebSocket /api/twin/ws)
LBL_SECURITY_TWINRELAY_HELP=Off by default: the socket then closes as if the twin were not configured. When on, the server opens the twin's own socket with the sign-in of each person and passes on only what the twin pushes; nothing a panel sends reaches the twin. It also needs the address of the twin on the server.
LBL_SECURITY_TRUSTED=Trusted networks
LBL_SECURITY_TRUSTED_ENABLED=Only allow administering the server from the house network and the VPN (outside, only accounts with the second factor can sign in)
LBL_SECURITY_TRUSTED_HELP=Off by default. When on, administering the server is refused from addresses outside the networks listed in the configuration file (the private ranges and the VPN); the policy for the rest is set there too. Check that you are on a trusted network before saving.
SECURITY_TRUSTED_WARNING=The server now refuses to be administered from outside the house network and the VPN.
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES=Machine bridges
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_HELP=Switches of the bridges that move or watch machines. Everything that moves hardware is off by default. The values are saved in the server and, while the gateway to the machine bridges is on, sent to each bridge; a bridge applies them only if its own host allows remote settings, otherwise it keeps what its own environment or file says.
SECURITY_BRIDGES_DELIVERY_ON=The gateway to the machine bridges is on: the values are sent to the bridges.
SECURITY_BRIDGES_DELIVERY_OFF=The gateway to the machine bridges is off: the values are saved but not sent until you switch it on.
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_DEFAULT=Default
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_LOCAL=Read on the bridge host as
SECURITY_BRIDGES_ON=On
SECURITY_BRIDGES_OFF=Off
MSG_SECURITY_BRIDGES_CONFIRM=One of these changes turns on a function that moves hardware or takes a protection away. Continue?
SECURITY_BRIDGES_WARNING=A bridge switch that moves hardware or lowers a protection was saved.
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_SIGNING=Signature of the settings sent to the bridges
SECURITY_BRIDGES_SIGNING_HELP=The settings are signed with one key per bridge, kept in a file on the server (never shown). Copy the key file to the host of the bridge and name it in the bridge's SETTINGS_KEY_FILE variable; a bridge applies a setting only when the signature is valid, current and not repeated.
SECURITY_BRIDGES_SIGNING_KEY_PRESENT=Key ready
SECURITY_BRIDGES_SIGNING_KEY_MISSING=No key yet (it is made when the settings are first sent)
SECURITY_BRIDGES_SIGNING_KEY_UNUSABLE=Key unusable: nothing is sent to this bridge
SECURITY_BRIDGES_SIGNING_LAST=Last signed
SECURITY_BRIDGES_SIGNING_NEVER=not yet
SECURITY_BRIDGES_SIGNING_FILE=Key file
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_OPT_DROIDS_GLOBAL_STOP=Obey the global stop (refuse jobs while the server announces a stop)
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_OPT_DROIDS_CUT=Cut the Spot session on a global stop
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_OPT_UAV_MISSION=Allow uploading a mission to the autopilot (does not start it)
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_OPT_DROIDS_CONFIRM=Require the confirmation of a person, signed by the server, before the droid walks, picks or places
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_OPT_DROIDS_HOME=Let going home through even if the droid still reports it is busy (never during a fault)
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_OPT_UAV_ENVELOPE=Require the flight envelope (ceiling and radius) before arming, taking off or going to a point
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_OPT_UAV_CONFIRM=Require the confirmation of a person, signed by the server, before arming, taking off or going to a point
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_OPT_UAV_CHAIN=Allow a go-to or a hover while the vehicle is already flying (after a successful request)
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_OPT_UAV_FENCE=Allow loading the radius of the envelope into the autopilot as a geofence
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_OPT_AMR_STATE=Publish the state of the vehicles
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_OPT_AMR_OPCUA=Publish the vehicles to the OPC UA server
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_OPT_AMR_INTERLOCK=Pause a vehicle whose next node is in an occupied zone
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_OPT_AMR_UNKNOWN=A zone whose occupancy is unknown counts as
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_OPT_OPENPNP_BOARD=Check the board code read from the board
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_CHOICE_PAUSE=Occupied (the vehicle waits)
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_CHOICE_IGNORE=Free (the vehicle goes on)
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_CHOICE_OFF=Off
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_CHOICE_ADVISORY=Advisory (warn only)
LBL_SECURITY_BRIDGES_CHOICE_REQUIRED=Required (refuse another board)
TITLE_SECURITY_BRIDGES=Machine bridges
LBL_SECURITY_RUL=Remaining useful life for operators
LBL_SECURITY_RUL_ENABLED=Let operators use the remaining-useful-life estimate of the AI dashboard (POST /api/ai/anomaly-detector/rul)
