PLAN_TITLE=Tier plan (data retention)
PLAN_DESC=How long the data lake keeps every raw point and how it rolls them up into wider buckets. The rules are strict: a plan that does not fit together cannot be saved.
PLAN_OFF=The data lake was not started with the plan administration (option --downsample-admin), so the plan cannot be edited from here.
PLAN_FORBIDDEN=Only an administrator can read or change the tier plan.
PLAN_UNREACHABLE=The data lake is not configured on this Server or does not answer.
PLAN_NETWORK=Could not reach the Server.
PLAN_MALFORMED=The data lake answered something this screen does not understand.
PLAN_HTTP=The data lake refused the request (HTTP {status}).
PLAN_RELOAD=Read again
PLAN_COL_KIND=Kind
PLAN_COL_FIELD=Field
PLAN_COL_RAW=Keep raw for
PLAN_COL_BUCKET=Rollup width
PLAN_COL_FINE=Narrow rollup width
PLAN_COL_KEEP=Keep rollups for
PLAN_COL_FINE_KEEP=Keep narrow rollups for
PLAN_ADD_TIER=Add tier
PLAN_REMOVE_TIER=Remove tier
PLAN_DURATION_HINT=Durations: 90s, 1m, 1h, 30d, 2w, 5y or milliseconds. Leave the optional cells empty. Kind * and field * is the default tier.
PLAN_DELETE_LABEL=Delete the raw points that were rolled up
PLAN_DELETE_DISABLED=Disabled: the operator has to start the data lake with --downsample-allow-delete. No request can switch it on.
PLAN_DELETE_WARNING=Rolled-up raw points are removed for good, and the rollups past their retention are removed too. Read the effects before saving.
PLAN_MODE_DRYRUN=Mode now: dry run (reports, deletes nothing)
PLAN_MODE_DELETE=Mode now: DELETING
PLAN_STRICT_NOTE=Strict rules, always on: the rollup width is not longer than the raw time, no retention is shorter than the raw time, the narrow retention is not longer than the rollup retention, the narrow width divides the rollup width, no tier is listed twice and every kind exists in the data lake. The data lake has no option to relax them.
PLAN_VALID=The plan is valid.
PLAN_INVALID_COUNT={count} problem(s): the plan cannot be saved.
PLAN_ROW=Row {row}
PLAN_PREVIEW=Check what it would do
PLAN_SAVE=Save plan
PLAN_SAVED=Plan saved. The timer uses it from its next round.
PLAN_UNCHANGED=Nothing changed: the data lake already has this plan.
PLAN_CONFIRM_TITLE=Save the tier plan?
PLAN_CONFIRM_MESSAGE=The data lake will use this plan from its next round. A saved plan never runs by itself.
PLAN_CONFIRM_DELETE_MESSAGE=This turns real deletion ON: the raw points that were rolled up will be removed for good. Are you sure?
PLAN_EFFECTS=Effects of the next round: {raw} raw point(s) to roll up, {rollups} rollup(s) and {fine} narrow rollup(s) to expire.
PLAN_CHANGES={count} tier(s) change.
PLAN_AUDIT_TITLE=Latest changes
PLAN_AUDIT_NONE=No changes recorded yet.
PLAN_AUDIT_ENTRY={event} from {client}, {tiers} tier(s)
PLAN_KNOWN_KINDS=Kinds in the data lake: {kinds}
PLAN_CONFIRM_SAVE=Save
PLAN_CONFIRM_CANCEL=Cancel
PLAN_PREVIEWED=Checked with the data lake: the plan is accepted.
PLAN_ERROR_PLAN_CHANGED=The plan changed since you read it. Read it again before saving.
PLAN_ERROR_CONFIRM_DELETE_REQUIRED=Turning deletion on needs your explicit confirmation after reading the effects.
PLAN_ERROR_DELETE_NOT_ALLOWED=The data lake was not started with --downsample-allow-delete, so a plan that deletes is refused.
PLAN_ERROR_INVALID_PLAN=The data lake rejected the shape of the plan.
PLAN_ERROR_INCOHERENT_PLAN=The widths or retentions of the plan do not fit together.
PLAN_ERROR_UNKNOWN_KIND=The plan names a kind this data lake does not know.
PLAN_ERROR_INVALID_REQUEST=The data lake did not understand the request.
PLAN_ERROR_WRITE_FAILED=The data lake could not write the plan; the old plan is untouched.
PLAN_ISSUE_NO_TIERS=The plan has no tiers.
PLAN_ISSUE_TOO_MANY_TIERS=At most {max} tiers.
PLAN_ISSUE_KIND_MISSING=The kind is empty.
PLAN_ISSUE_FIELD_MISSING=The field is empty.
PLAN_ISSUE_DEFAULT_NEEDS_STAR_FIELD=A field needs a kind: only the default tier is * and *.
PLAN_ISSUE_DUPLICATE={kind}/{field} is listed twice.
PLAN_ISSUE_REQUIRED=This duration is required.
PLAN_ISSUE_BAD_DURATION={value} is not a duration such as 90s, 1h, 30d or 5y.
PLAN_ISSUE_FINE_NOT_SMALLER=The narrow width must be smaller than the rollup width.
PLAN_ISSUE_FINE_NOT_DIVISOR=The narrow width must divide the rollup width exactly.
PLAN_ISSUE_FINE_TOO_MANY=At most {max} narrow buckets per rollup bucket.
PLAN_ISSUE_FINE_RETENTION_NEEDS_FINE=The narrow retention needs a narrow width.
PLAN_ISSUE_FINE_RETENTION_ON_DEFAULT=The narrow retention is not available on the default tier.
PLAN_ISSUE_FINE_RETENTION_LONGER=The narrow retention must not be longer than the rollup retention.
PLAN_ISSUE_BUCKET_LONGER_THAN_RAW=The rollup width must not be longer than the raw time.
PLAN_ISSUE_ROLLUP_SHORTER_THAN_RAW=The rollup retention must not be shorter than the raw time.
PLAN_ISSUE_FINE_RETENTION_SHORTER_THAN_RAW=The narrow retention must not be shorter than the raw time.
PLAN_ISSUE_UNKNOWN_KIND=The kind {kind} has no data and no policy in this data lake.
HEADING_FW_SIG=Firmware signature check (this computer)
LBL_FW_SIG_VERIFY=Verify the Ed25519 signature of a firmware image here before sending it to the flashing service
LBL_FW_SIG_KEY_FILE=Public key file (32 bytes as 64 hexadecimal digits)
PH_FW_SIG_KEY_FILE=Path of the public key file
LBL_FW_SIG_FINGERPRINT=Key fingerprint (SHA-256, first 128 bits)
LBL_FW_SIG_HELP=Only the path of the key file is saved in the configuration file, never the key. An image that is unsigned, has a bad signature or belongs to an unknown board is refused with the reason. The bootloader checks the signature again.
TITLE_FW_SIG_OFF=Turn off the signature check?
MSG_FW_SIG_OFF_CONFIRM=Firmware images will be sent to the flashing service without being checked on this computer. Only the bootloader of the board will still check them.
FW_SIG_KEY_LOADED=Key loaded
FW_SIG_NO_KEY=The public key file is missing or cannot be read
FW_SIG_KEY_BAD=The public key file does not hold a key (it must have 64 hexadecimal digits)
FW_SIG_UNSIGNED=the image has no signature
FW_SIG_NO_VERSION=the version of the image is unknown
FW_SIG_NO_HARDWARE=the board of the image is unknown (a file picked from disk has no board or version)
FW_SIG_IMAGE_SHORT=the image is too short
FW_SIG_BAD=the signature does not match this image and key
FW_SIG_OK=Signature verified on this computer
FW_SIG_OFF=The signature check is off
FW_SIG_WARNING_OFF=The signature check is OFF: images are not verified on this computer.
FW_SIG_OFF_LOG=Warning: the signature check is off, the image was not verified here
FW_SIG_REFUSED=Image refused, not sent
FW_SIG_SAVED=Signature settings saved

HUBGATE_TITLE=Connector hub: callers without identity
HUBGATE_DESC=The decision gate of the connector hub answers only callers that present a signed token of this server. This switch lets a caller on the hub's own machine be answered without a token. It is off by default; only an administrator can change it, turning it on asks for a confirmation, and every change is recorded.
HUBGATE_LABEL=Answer a caller on the hub's own machine without a token
HUBGATE_STATE_ON=On: a caller on the hub's machine is answered without identity.
HUBGATE_STATE_OFF=Off: every caller needs a signed token (default).
HUBGATE_FORBIDDEN=Only an administrator can read or change this switch.
HUBGATE_LOAD_ERROR=Could not read the switch of the connector hub gate.
HUBGATE_SAVE_ERROR=The change was refused: {reason}
HUBGATE_LOOPBACK_ONLY=The hub does not listen on a loopback address, so the switch cannot be turned on.
HUBGATE_NEEDS_KEY=The hub has no key that verifies tokens, so the switch cannot be turned off from here.
HUBGATE_KEPT_FILE=The change is kept in the settings file of the hub across restarts.
HUBGATE_KEPT_MEMORY=The change lasts until the hub restarts (the hub has no settings file).
HUBGATE_CONFIRM_TITLE=Turn on answers without identity?
HUBGATE_CONFIRM_MESSAGE=Anything that runs on the hub's machine will be able to ask the gate for decisions without a signed token. Turn this on only on a machine you control.

PLANNERID_TITLE=Semantic planner: who approves a plan
PLANNERID_DESC=The semantic planner releases a plan only when the person who approves it is signed in with a token of this server and is the person named in the approval. This switch relaxes that for a bench without the server. It is on by default; only an administrator can change it, relaxing it asks for a confirmation, and every change is recorded.
PLANNERID_LABEL=Require a signed-in operator to approve a plan
PLANNERID_STATE_ON=On: the approval is made by the person who is signed in (default).
PLANNERID_STATE_OFF=Off: the approval is the words of the request (only for a bench).
PLANNERID_UNSUPPORTED=This server does not offer the settings of the semantic planner.
PLANNERID_NOT_CONFIGURED=The semantic planner is not set up on this server.
PLANNERID_FORBIDDEN=Only an administrator can read or change this switch.
PLANNERID_LOAD_ERROR=Could not read the identity switch of the semantic planner.
PLANNERID_NEEDS_KEY=The planner has no identity key, so the switch cannot be changed from here.
PLANNERID_KEPT_FILE=The change is kept in the configuration file of the planner across restarts.
PLANNERID_KEPT_MEMORY=The change lasts until the planner restarts (it has no configuration file).
PLANNERID_SAVE_ERROR=The change was refused: {reason}
PLANNERID_CONFIRM_TITLE=Relax the identity of the approval?
PLANNERID_CONFIRM_MESSAGE=Plans will be released on the words of the request, without the person being signed in. Relax this only on a bench without the server.

SERVICEID_TITLE=Identity of the services
SERVICEID_DESC=This server can present a short signed token of its own on every call it makes to the services (status scan, health probes, relays, stop relay). A service whose identity key is on refuses a call that carries none. It is off by default; only an administrator can change it, turning it on asks for a confirmation and every change is recorded.
SERVICEID_LABEL=Present the identity of this server to the services
SERVICEID_STATE_PRESENTING=On: the server is presenting its signed token.
SERVICEID_STATE_OFF=Off: the calls of the server carry no identity (default).
SERVICEID_STATE_IDLE_NO_KEY=On, but nothing can be signed: JWT_SECRET is unset, an example value or too short.
SERVICEID_LOCKED=Set in the environment of the server (HYDRA_UMC_SERVICE_IDENTITY): remove it there to change it here.
SERVICEID_SERVICES_TITLE=Services
SERVICEID_ACCEPTS=Accept the identity
SERVICEID_OWN_VERIFIER=Keep a verifier of their own
SERVICEID_NOT_YET=Do not accept it yet
SERVICEID_NONE=none
SERVICEID_ORDER_TITLE=Safe order
SERVICEID_ORDER_1=1. Turn this switch on first, so that the server presents its token.
SERVICEID_ORDER_2=2. Then give the key to the services one by one: as root on the machine, run provisioning/service_identity.py --enable NAME --apply of HYDRA-UMC-OS, restart that unit and check it with --status. This screen never does it.
SERVICEID_ORDER_3=Turning the key on in a service before the server presents its token makes that service refuse the server.
SERVICEID_SAVED=Saved.
SERVICEID_SAVE_ERROR=The change was refused: {reason}
SERVICEID_UNSUPPORTED=This server does not offer the identity of the services.
SERVICEID_FORBIDDEN=Only an administrator can read or change this switch.
SERVICEID_LOAD_ERROR=The identity of the services could not be read.
SERVICEID_OFF_WARNING=Off: a service whose identity key is on will refuse this server. Turn the keys off in those services first.
SERVICEID_CONFIRM_TITLE=Turn on the identity of the server?
SERVICEID_CONFIRM_MESSAGE=The server will present a signed token on its calls to the services. Turn it on before giving the identity key to any service, and give the keys one service at a time.

OPSPROP_TITLE=Node watchdog: proposals waiting for a person
OPSPROP_DESC=The node watchdog never opens a maintenance incident from a proposal on its own: each one waits here until an administrator approves or rejects it. Approving asks for a confirmation and every decision is recorded under your name.
OPSPROP_NONE=No proposal is waiting.
OPSPROP_META={id} - node {node} - severity {severity} - detected {at}
OPSPROP_REJECT=Reject
OPSPROP_REFRESH=Refresh
OPSPROP_APPROVED=Approved: {id}.
OPSPROP_REJECTED=Rejected: {id}.
OPSPROP_DECIDED_APPROVED=Approved {id} by {by} ({at})
OPSPROP_DECIDED_REJECTED=Rejected {id} by {by} ({at})
OPSPROP_UNSUPPORTED=This server does not offer the proposals of the node watchdog.
OPSPROP_NOT_CONFIGURED=The node watchdog is not configured on this server.
OPSPROP_FORBIDDEN=Only an administrator can read or decide the proposals.
OPSPROP_NOT_PENDING=That proposal is no longer waiting.
OPSPROP_LOAD_ERROR=The proposals of the node watchdog could not be read.
OPSPROP_DECIDE_ERROR=The decision was refused: {reason}
OPSPROP_CONFIRM_TITLE=Approve this proposal?
OPSPROP_CONFIRM_MESSAGE=Approving {id} opens it as a maintenance incident. The decision is recorded under your name.
OPSPROP_CONFIRM_BUTTON=Approve

HILBRIDGE_TITLE=HIL bridge: pass verdict of the twin
HILBRIDGE_DESC=When this is on, the HIL bridge moves the real robot only for a command whose trajectory the twin passed in simulation (a signed verdict, checked against the exact points). It is off by default; only an administrator can change it, a confirmation is needed in both directions and every change is recorded.
HILBRIDGE_LABEL=Require a pass verdict of the twin before the real robot moves
HILBRIDGE_STATE_ON=On: a real command needs the pass verdict of the twin for its trajectory.
HILBRIDGE_STATE_OFF=Off: a real command needs only its risk certificate (the default).
HILBRIDGE_UNSUPPORTED=This server does not offer the settings of the HIL bridge.
HILBRIDGE_NOT_CONFIGURED=The HIL bridge is not configured on this server.
HILBRIDGE_FORBIDDEN=Only an administrator can change this switch.
HILBRIDGE_LOAD_ERROR=The switch of the HIL bridge could not be read.
HILBRIDGE_LOCKED=The bridge was started with this switch locked on, so it cannot be turned off from here.
HILBRIDGE_NOT_READY=The bridge has no twin key or no robot set, so the switch cannot be turned on yet.
HILBRIDGE_NO_IDENTITY=The bridge does not have the identity key of this server, so the switch cannot be changed from here.
HILBRIDGE_KEPT_FILE=The change is kept in the file of the bridge after restarts.
HILBRIDGE_KEPT_MEMORY=The change lasts until the bridge restarts (it has no file for it).
HILBRIDGE_SAVE=Save
HILBRIDGE_SAVED=Saved.
HILBRIDGE_SAVE_ERROR=The change was refused: {reason}
HILBRIDGE_CONFIRM_ON_TITLE=Require the verdict of the twin?
HILBRIDGE_CONFIRM_ON_MESSAGE=From now on the HIL bridge will refuse every real command that does not carry a pass verdict of the twin for its trajectory.
HILBRIDGE_CONFIRM_ON_BUTTON=Require
HILBRIDGE_CONFIRM_OFF_TITLE=Stop requiring the verdict of the twin?
HILBRIDGE_CONFIRM_OFF_MESSAGE=The HIL bridge will forward real commands with only their risk certificate, without a pass verdict of the twin for the trajectory.
HILBRIDGE_CONFIRM_OFF_BUTTON=Stop requiring
