SETUP_REMOTE_CLOSE_ALL=Close all
SETUP_REMOTE_CLOSE_ALL_CONFIRM=Every kind of app will stop finding this server. Apps that are already connected may need to sign in again. Continue?
SETUP_REMOTE_STEP3=3. Check from the phone
SETUP_REMOTE_STEP3_HINT=Put the phone on the same network, open the app and let it search or type the address. If it does not find the server, check that its kind of app is turned on above and that nothing blocks the connection on the network.
SETUP_NOTIFICATIONS_TITLE=Push notifications
SETUP_NOTIFICATIONS_INTRO=The warnings the server sends to the phones that registered with it: whether they are on, whether they can be sent and which events are announced.
SETUP_NOTIFICATIONS_ADMIN_ONLY=Only administrators can see the state of the notifications.
SETUP_NOTIFICATIONS_VERDICT_OFF=Push notifications are off on this server.
SETUP_NOTIFICATIONS_VERDICT_NEEDS_CREDENTIALS=Push notifications are on, but the server cannot send them: its credentials are missing or not usable.
SETUP_NOTIFICATIONS_VERDICT_READY=Push notifications are on and ready to be sent.
SETUP_NOTIFICATIONS_SANDBOX=It uses the test host of the Apple push service.
SETUP_NOTIFICATIONS_EVENT_JOBFINISHED=A job finished
SETUP_NOTIFICATIONS_EVENT_GLOBALSTOP=A global stop was issued
SETUP_NOTIFICATIONS_EVENT_OPERATORHEARTBEATLOST=The signal of an operator was lost
SETUP_ON=on
SETUP_OFF=off
SETUP_HISTORY_TITLE=What happened and when
SETUP_HISTORY_INTRO=Who connected to the server and, for an administrator, the record of the changes that matter.
SETUP_HISTORY_PART_CONNECTIONS=Connections
SETUP_HISTORY_PART_AUDIT=Audit record
SETUP_HISTORY_AUDIT_ADMIN_ONLY=The audit record is only shown to administrators.
SETUP_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED=This server does not offer this information (it predates the route).
SETUP_ERROR_FORBIDDEN=Your account is not allowed to read this. Sign in as an administrator.
SETUP_ERROR_HTTP=The server answered with an error. Try again in a moment.
SETUP_ERROR_NETWORK=The server cannot be reached. Check the connection.
SETUP_VERSIONS_INTRO=The version of this Suite, the one of the server and the version each program next to the server reports.
SETUP_VERSIONS_SUITE=This Suite
SETUP_VERSIONS_NO_SOURCE=This server has no route that tells which version is the newest or that installs one, so this screen only shows what is installed and changes nothing. Updates are made with the updater of each program.
SETUP_SECURITY_ALLOW_ROTATION=Allow rotating the key from this screen (off every time this screen is opened)
SETUP_SECURITY_TOTP_WHERE=The two-step sign-in of your account is set up on the Server admin screen.
SETUP_INSTALLATION_STEP_CONTROLLER_HINT=Add a controller with the name and IP address of its board in HYDRA-UMC STUDIO.
SETUP_INSTALLATION_STEP_ROBOT_HINT=Pick a robot slot of the controller and choose its model and tool.
SETUP_INSTALLATION_STEP_SECOND_FACTOR_HINT=Server admin screen. It is optional and off until you turn it on.
SETUP_REMOTE_INTRO=Lets the Android and iOS apps, the watch, the DSI screen and the desktop SUITE find this server.
SETUP_REMOTE_LOCAL_WARNING=This Suite reaches the server as localhost (this same machine): a phone cannot use this address. Connect to the server by the name or IP address of the machine and come back here.
SETUP_REMOTE_ADDRESS=Address
SETUP_NOTIFICATIONS_READ_ONLY=This screen only shows the state. The server reads these switches from its own security file (push notifications are off until an administrator turns them on there) and has no route to change them or to mute one event, so there are no switches here.
