PREFS_TOURS_TITLE=Offer the guided tours
PREFS_TOURS_HINT=Shows the Guided tour entries in the application menu and on the screens that have one. Turning it off closes a tour that is open. Kept in the configuration file of this program only.
TOUR_WELCOME_0_T=Welcome to HYDRA-UMC SUITE
TOUR_WELCOME_0_B=This short tour shows where things are. You can close it at any time with Esc and start it again from the application menu.
TOUR_WELCOME_1_T=The menu
TOUR_WELCOME_1_B=Everything is reached from the list on the left: the robots, the tools, the screens of the ecosystem and the settings of the server.
TOUR_WELCOME_2_T=Ecosystem health
TOUR_WELCOME_2_B=The state of each service of the ecosystem, the version it reports against the one expected, and the controller boards as the brain heard them.
TOUR_WELCOME_3_T=Server Admin
TOUR_WELCOME_3_B=The users, the security options and the switches of the server. Everything risky is off until an administrator turns it on.
TOUR_WELCOME_4_T=STOP
TOUR_WELCOME_4_B=The stop button is always in sight: one click stops every robot. F12 does the same from the keyboard.
TOUR_HEALTH_0_T=Services
TOUR_HEALTH_0_B=Each card is one service with its state, the version it reports against the one expected and when it last answered.
TOUR_HEALTH_1_T=Controller boards
TOUR_HEALTH_1_B=Below the services, the last health frame the brain heard from each controller board. This part appears only when an administrator turned the option on.
SELFUPD_TITLE=HYDRA-UMC updates
SELFUPD_INTRO=The server, Studio and the agent of the operating system, set against the newest signed release of each. The server fetches the package, its hash and its signature from the release, checks them with the signature check of the releases of HYDRA-UMC and installs the program next to the one in use, which is kept as the earlier release. Only the program that changes is restarted, never the machine.
SELFUPD_SWITCH_TITLE=Allow applying updates from this program
SELFUPD_SWITCH_HINT=Off: this screen only looks for newer versions. On: you can update a program or put its earlier release back, always after a confirmation. Kept in the configuration file of this program only.
SELFUPD_UNSUPPORTED=This server does not offer the update of its programs: an administrator has to switch on the look at the newest versions in Server Admin (and, to apply, the maintenance routes).
SELFUPD_FORBIDDEN=Only an administrator can see this; sign in again with an administrator account.
SELFUPD_LOAD_ERROR=The versions could not be read from the server. Try again in a moment.
SELFUPD_CHECK=Check now
SELFUPD_COL_PROGRAM=Program
SELFUPD_COL_INSTALLED=Installed
SELFUPD_COL_PREVIOUS=Earlier release
SELFUPD_COL_LATEST=Newest signed
SELFUPD_COL_STATE=State
SELFUPD_STATE_CURRENT=up to date
SELFUPD_STATE_BEHIND=update available
SELFUPD_STATE_AHEAD=newer than the release
SELFUPD_STATE_UNKNOWN=not known
SELFUPD_NO_PACKAGE=the release has no signed package
SELFUPD_UPDATE=Update
SELFUPD_ROLLBACK=Go back
SELFUPD_MODE_CHECK_ONLY=Check only: nothing is installed from here until you allow it above.
SELFUPD_MODE_APPLY=Applying is allowed: every update and every way back asks you first.
SELFUPD_MODE_SERVER_OFF=The server has applying switched off (maintenance routes in Server Admin), so nothing can be installed from here.
SELFUPD_RATE_LIMITED=GitHub refused for quota: some newest versions are not known yet.
SELFUPD_COMPONENT_SERVER=Server
SELFUPD_COMPONENT_STUDIO=Studio
SELFUPD_COMPONENT_OS_AGENT=Agent of the operating system
SELFUPD_CONFIRM_TITLE=Confirm the update
SELFUPD_CONFIRM_APPLY=Update {program} ({versions})? The signed package will be fetched, checked and installed, and only this program will restart.
SELFUPD_CONFIRM_ROLLBACK=Put the earlier release of {program} back ({versions})? Only this program will restart.
SELFUPD_CONFIRM_NOTE=If the new release does not start or does not pass its health check, the earlier one is put back by itself.
SELFUPD_START_DISABLED=The server has applying switched off.
SELFUPD_START_FORBIDDEN=Only an administrator can do this, and listen-only mode never does; sign in again.
SELFUPD_START_BUSY=Another update is going on, or there is no earlier release to go back to.
SELFUPD_START_REFUSED=The server refused to start it.
SELFUPD_START_NETWORK=The server could not be reached.
SELFUPD_JOB_APPLY=Updating {program}
SELFUPD_JOB_ROLLBACK=Putting the earlier release of {program} back
SELFUPD_STEP_CHECKING=Checking
SELFUPD_STEP_DOWNLOADING=Downloading
SELFUPD_STEP_VERIFYING=Verifying signature and hash
SELFUPD_STEP_APPLYING=Applying
SELFUPD_STEP_RESTARTING=Restarting the program
SELFUPD_STEP_DONE=Done
SELFUPD_DONE_APPLY=Done: version {version} is in use.
SELFUPD_DONE_ROLLBACK=Done: back on version {version}.
SELFUPD_WAITING=The server is restarting; waiting for it to answer ({seconds} s). The update goes on without this window.
SELFUPD_GAVE_UP=The server has not answered for a long time. The update may have finished or may still be going on.
SELFUPD_LOOK_AGAIN=Look again
SELFUPD_ERR_GENERIC=The update failed.
SELFUPD_ERR_NO_RELEASE=No release could be read from GitHub.
SELFUPD_ERR_ALREADY_CURRENT=This program is already on the newest release.
SELFUPD_ERR_NO_SIGNED_PACKAGE=The newest release has no signed package for this program.
SELFUPD_ERR_DOWNLOAD_FAILED=The download failed or was cut. Nothing was installed.
SELFUPD_ERR_PACKAGE_TOO_LARGE=The package is larger than the limit. Nothing was installed.
SELFUPD_ERR_SIGNATURE_INVALID=The hash or the signature of the package did not hold. It was discarded and nothing was installed.
SELFUPD_ERR_NO_EARLIER_RELEASE=There is no earlier release to go back to.
SELFUPD_ERR_START_FAILED=The update could not be started.
SELFUPD_ERR_ROLLED_BACK=The new release did not hold; the earlier one was put back and is running.
SELFUPD_ERR_DEPLOY_FAILED=The installation failed. Look at the detail below.
SELFUPD_ERR_TIMEOUT=The installer did not report an end in time. Check the state of the program.
SELFUPD_ERR_INTERRUPTED=The server was restarted before the package was in place. Nothing was installed.
HELP_SELFUPDATE_Q=How do I update the programs of the machine, and go back if something fails?
HELP_SELFUPDATE_S1=Open {eco} > {selfupdate} as an administrator and find the section HYDRA-UMC updates. It lists the server, Studio and the agent of the operating system with the installed, the earlier and the newest signed version; Check now reads them again.
HELP_SELFUPDATE_S2=Applying is off until you allow it with the switch on that screen, and the server must allow it too. Then Update and Go back appear, each after a confirmation that names the program and the two versions.
HELP_SELFUPDATE_S3=The job shows its steps. The server restarts in the middle of its own update, so the screen keeps asking and says it is waiting; after four minutes of silence it offers Look again. A failure says why and what was put back.
